  "doc.title": "How Chips Share Memory · a long essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "A server's CPU, GPUs, accelerators and memory-expansion cards each have their own memory. Why do they all want to share one, how is a cache kept coherent across a PCIe wire, and how are dozens of GPUs joined into one machine? Nine hands-on models: copy or share, the slot accounting of CXL flits, the messages of the three device types, memory expansion and hot/cold tiering, memory pooling, back-invalidate, ring all-reduce step by step, how long an all-reduce takes, and scale-up versus scale-out; plus an NVLink table and coherence inside one package.",
